title The fire row cuts three bodies to one -- the enclosure door, fifteen shims, and the almanac engine land parity-proven
prompt Keaton granted the recommended doors across four messages, asked whether lexicon, almanac, PLEAC, docs-geode, and the rota docs are too similar, asked for a single-stranded reading of the artifacts, and asked the new bodies to carry fascia -- kin links back home.
think The fire triad read: the threshold (vision -- the lap that sees clearly cuts once), and the three depths (molt readies, breach renames, debride removes; cut exactly as deep as the truth requires). Standfast and reds-first are held from constant application this session -- three reds booked under them today -- said here honestly rather than reread whole. The whole movement then WAS the row's teaching: every cut below was proven from both sides before it landed.
think The enclosure door: the eight-line ENCLOSURE admission gate stood in three launchers sharing ZERO literal lines -- idea sameness, the kind no diff sees -- so tools/e/enclosure_gate.sh now holds it once (read selector, admit pond only behind pond_exit_bron_master_seal.sh --require, refuse anything else, print the admitted word), each launcher makes one call, and the door's four legs ran on metal before any launcher moved. The seal-gate scan needed zero logic changes; its prose, the witness pin (sealed_gates 3 to 1), and the control (pen gains the door; the elder gate planted back into the example case so the bare-name rule keeps a live subject) moved in the same commit. Scan green, control 42 of 42, witness GREEN. When Pond lands, retiring ai-jail is one deletion in one file.
think The wire-labs: an agent survey found the family already half-condensed -- 15 shims of one 8-line body each exec-ing a per-lab tools/co orchestrator, the lab a pure function of the basename. One runner (comlink/run_wire_lab.sh, lab as argument, roster read live from tools/co) plus 15 four-line shims keeping their names and their one-line accounts; 15 living callers untouched; 173 lines to 60. The runner stays .sh for a named reason: Rishi binds a script no dollar-zero, so only a POSIX shim self-locates -- the bootstrap seam the molt rule honestly stops at.
think The almanac: 114 append scripts, one body -- and generation by execution rather than hand-parsing. Bumps read from each elder's own python AST and reverse-applied so both runs FIRE them; entries recovered from what the elder actually inserted; stamps mapped to placeholders by clock-bracketing. Four legs per member in pens (append byte-identical after stamp normalization, steady untouched, marker refusal both shapes); first run flagged one census member whose pen starved its scan -- the pen widened to symlink every room and 114 of 114 proved. Installed through the tracked inodes; all 114 answer already-present on the real tree with the book unchanged; the map witness runs GREEN through its stub; 4,639 lines to 1,410.
think The doc survey answered Keaton's question with a measured no: lexicon (name ledger), almanac (findings ledger), PLEAC (cookbook), docs-geode (crushed shipping shelf), rota (curriculum) serve five readers and cross-cite rather than restate; the five rota thresholds share a 6-heading template with 93 to 95 percent unique prose -- deliberate curriculum, declined for merging. The real debts were internal: GLOW_ALMANAC's charter promised closure at sixty-four findings while the book holds 127 (repaired with a dated amendment -- a close waits on a word, not a count); LEXICON's Lap row disagreed with the daily-words foundation (repointed); LEXICON at 187KB wants condense-on-touch, rows carrying history that belongs on shelves.
obs Single-stranded reading, the pull test on each new body: the door pulls free (delete it and three launchers fail loudly at one line rather than drifting); the runner pulls free (shims are pure names); the engine separates data from body so each stub is ONLY its data. The braids that remain are named, not hidden: the QEMU incantation repeated about 46 times inside tools/co, the almanac family's entanglement with the witness choir and the %330 rename, and LEXICON rows doing two jobs. Fascia seated: all three new bodies carry KIN blocks pointing home -- seal, guard, quest, and card for the door; orchestrators and the molt rule for the runner; the book, the choir, and %330 for the engine.
obs Fleet discipline held: the peer's staged lap was never touched; four pathspec commits; the amend guard refused once over the peer's cached diff and was honored (the runner's exec bit rides this closing slice instead); the roster cold/hot run was skipped for the seated reason -- two seats cannot roster one tree, and the peer's lap is open. The day-index row follows the peer's landing, promptly, as the shelf law asks. A red candidate for the next lap, fetch-first once the ledger frees: the charter that outran itself -- a bound written in prose with no meter is a wish, the %83 class one room over.
